# ==============================================================================
# Tender Pocket — PostgreSQL Backup & Automated Restore Verification Crontab
# ==============================================================================
# Target Environment: AWS EC2 Ubuntu Host (/home/ubuntu/tender-pocket)
# Times: written in UTC (the EC2 clock), shown in IST in the comments. See "SCHEDULE" below.
# Dedicated S3 Bucket: POSTGRES_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET (e.g. tender-pocket-postgres-backups)
#
# Pre-requisites on EC2 host before installation:
#   1. Ensure logs directory exists and is writable:
#      mkdir -p /home/ubuntu/tender-pocket/logs
#      chmod 755 /home/ubuntu/tender-pocket/logs
#   2. Ensure backup scripts are executable:
#      chmod +x /home/ubuntu/tender-pocket/scripts/postgres-backup-*.py
#   3. Verify Docker container 'tender-pocket-postgres' is accessible:
#      docker exec -i tender-pocket-postgres pg_isready -U postgres
#   4. Verify AWS IAM Instance Profile / CLI credentials have PutObject & HeadObject
#      permissions on the destination S3 bucket:
#      aws s3 ls s3://tender-pocket-postgres-backups/
#   5. Install into active user crontab:
#      crontab -e
#      (Paste the block below, verifying PROJECT_DIR matches deployment path)
#   6. Verify installation:
#      crontab -l
#   7. Check the server clock is UTC (the times below assume it):
#      timedatectl | grep "Time zone"        -> Etc/UTC (UTC, +0000)
#   8. Set PROJECT_DIR below to the folder that holds docker-compose.yml. To find it:
#      docker inspect tender-pocket-backend --format '{{ index .Config.Labels "com.docker.compose.project.working_dir" }}'
#
# SCHEDULE:
#   The EC2 server is stopped every night from 22:00 to 07:00 IST by EventBridge Scheduler
#   (DEPLOYMENT.md section 46). A job set inside that window never runs, so all three jobs run
#   between 21:00 and 21:30 IST, while PostgreSQL is still up.
#   Ubuntu's cron ignores CRON_TZ and uses the server clock, which is UTC on EC2. So the times
#   are written in UTC: IST = UTC + 5:30, and 21:00 IST is 15:30 UTC on the same date.
#
# IMPORTANT OPERATIONAL NOTE:
#   This file is a reference sample only. Having this sample file present in the
#   repository is NOT proof that automatic scheduling is installed or active on EC2.
#   Scheduling is only active after manual installation via `crontab -e` on the host.
# ==============================================================================

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/sbin
PROJECT_DIR=/home/ubuntu/tender-pocket

# 1. Daily Full PostgreSQL Backup (Includes weekly recovery point archiving on Sundays)
# Executes every day at 21:00 IST (15:30 UTC), before the 22:00 IST server stop
30 15 * * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && /usr/bin/env python3 $PROJECT_DIR/scripts/postgres-backup-daily.py >> $PROJECT_DIR/logs/backup-daily.log 2>&1

# 2. Monthly Full PostgreSQL Backup
# Executes on the 1st of every month at 21:20 IST (15:50 UTC)
50 15 1 * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && /usr/bin/env python3 $PROJECT_DIR/scripts/postgres-backup-monthly.py >> $PROJECT_DIR/logs/backup-monthly.log 2>&1

# 3. Monthly Isolated Restore Verification Test
# Executes on the 2nd of every month at 21:30 IST (16:00 UTC). It restores the newest local
# backup into a scratch database (never the live one), so on the 2nd it tests that day's
# 21:00 backup. It runs on the 2nd so it does not overlap the 1st's monthly backup.
0 16 2 * * cd $PROJECT_DIR && /usr/bin/env python3 $PROJECT_DIR/scripts/postgres-restore-test.py >> $PROJECT_DIR/logs/restore-test.log 2>&1
